{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he shall judge.</b> The judge, and he is the Messiah, like 'whom she bore to Levi' (Numbers 26:59)." "<b>Into picks.</b> Like 'his mattock' and 'his pick' (1 Samuel 13:20). And the dagesh in the tav is for the missing alef that is in the word אתו." "<b>Into pruning-hooks.</b> With which the vinedressers prune."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:33.245620387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}